Brief thought on math vs. Go.
Quoting @littmath
@GregHBurnham @Miles_Brundage Yes indeed. One salient difference is that the objects involved in Go don’t change/expand. But in math we’re constantly thinking about new objects and questions of interest. Big question is whether this is more analogous to “new Go positions” or “different board game.”

